## Hints for Future Agents
- ccusage costs are computed at print time from cached TOKEN COUNTS, not cached
  dollar amounts. So a pricing.go change takes effect on the next normal run —
  no --no-cache / --clear-cache needed.
- For AllRegular AND AllFast to both resolve, a new model needs BOTH a base key
  and a `:fast` key. Base only -> AllFast falls back to regular; :fast only ->
  AllRegular falls back to default.
- Map keys with brackets ("opus[1m]") are valid Go string literals; build is fine.
- Opus 4.8 logs as plain `claude-opus-4-8` (no date suffix, like 4.6/4.7). The
  short `opus[1m]` alias is the 1M-context invocation form. ccusage has NO
  per-request context-length tiering, so opus[1m] is priced flat as Opus 4.8
  (no long-context premium modeled).

## Codebase Discoveries
- Repo has zero test files; verification is build + vet + manual run only.
- Opus 4.5/4.6/4.7 all share identical rates ($5/$25 reg, $30/$150 fast). 4.8 is
  the first to diverge: fast dropped to $10/$50.
- Lowering generic opus:fast re-prices historical plain-`opus` fast usage at the
  new rate, but only ~5 such entries exist; impact negligible. User chose this so
